WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:07.960
Playing at Hillsdale was probably the best
four years of my life.

00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:10.450
It was team, family.

00:00:10.450 --> 00:00:12.430
The atmosphere was just family.

00:00:12.430 --> 00:00:14.809
Coach Dick Lowry came in, and that was his
first year.

00:00:14.809 --> 00:00:16.580
That was his first recruiting class.

00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:20.699
We won the GLIAC Championship in 1980, my
freshman year.

00:00:20.699 --> 00:00:24.579
It got Hillsdale back on the map for football.

00:00:24.579 --> 00:00:28.550
Coach preached family, and discipline, and
character.

00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:31.989
The friends I have are like brothers.

00:00:31.989 --> 00:00:38.300
The most impactful person besides my father
and my mom but from the college was Coach

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:41.560
McAvoy who was like a second father.

00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:43.989
Two weeks into my freshman year, I came in.

00:00:43.989 --> 00:00:45.280
I was out of shape.

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:46.539
I wanted to go home.

00:00:46.539 --> 00:00:50.720
Coach Mac saw me walking back to
Simpson Dorm and said, "What are you doing?"

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:51.720
I said, "I'm going home.

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:52.720
I, I'm embarrassed.

00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:53.720
I can't get my equipment."

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:54.720
I'll never forget it.

00:00:54.720 --> 00:01:00.429
He said, "Just remember that the decision
you make today will impact you and your family

00:01:00.429 --> 00:01:01.589
for the rest of your life."

00:01:01.589 --> 00:01:04.769
He said, "You know, the coaches brought you
here because they had a belief in you.

00:01:04.769 --> 00:01:07.480
You've got to find that inside yourself.

00:01:07.480 --> 00:01:11.110
Believe that you can do it, and, and prove
them, prove them right."

00:01:11.110 --> 00:01:16.380
One conversation from Coach Mac
changed my life.

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:18.920
Started three years, was elected to captain.

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:22.640
Being elected captain by your teammates was
a very humbling moment.

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:25.729
Made All-Conference, All-District, All-American.

00:01:25.729 --> 00:01:28.240
To sign an NFL contract was a dream.

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:32.781
I wasn't fortunate enough to make the final
roster for Detroit or Pittsburgh, but I had

00:01:32.781 --> 00:01:36.479
two years in camps and preseason.

00:01:36.479 --> 00:01:40.700
I can always look back and say, "I tried and
I gave it all I had."

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:42.409
To me, that was good enough.

00:01:42.409 --> 00:01:47.680
The other person that made a difference in
my life was Keith Otterbein, our current head

00:01:47.680 --> 00:01:48.909
football coach.

00:01:48.909 --> 00:01:53.250
Otter reached out to me and asked me what
my plans were.

00:01:53.250 --> 00:01:54.719
I didn't really have any plans.

00:01:54.719 --> 00:02:00.200
I was reeling from the loss of my brother,
Bob, and coached reached out to me and gave

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:03.220
me an opportunity to come up to Ferris
and become a coach.

00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:06.700
I coached for four years as defensive line
coach.

00:02:06.700 --> 00:02:08.289
I was a strength coordinator.

00:02:08.289 --> 00:02:11.820
Otter reached out to me at the lowest times
of my life and saved me.

00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:18.540
The thing I miss most about coaching is how
you can influence somebody's life.

00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:21.980
I had an opportunity to coach at the youth
level, high school, college.

00:02:21.980 --> 00:02:26.150
Probably the greatest thing I still get is
when I run into former players and I hear,

00:02:26.150 --> 00:02:27.150
"Coach."

00:02:27.150 --> 00:02:28.150
I love it.

00:02:28.150 --> 00:02:33.420
Being elected into the Hillsdale College Athletic
Hall of Fame is unfathomable.

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:35.170
When I made All-American, I thought that was
it.

00:02:35.170 --> 00:02:36.959
It doesn't get much better than that.

00:02:36.959 --> 00:02:40.670
I've been out of school since 1984.

00:02:40.670 --> 00:02:44.710
You see the people up ... I've been back to
a couple Hall of Fame inductions.

00:02:44.710 --> 00:02:49.980
To be considered the best of the best that
have ever played at Hillsdale, it's an honor.

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:52.069
It's hard to put into words.

